Platform driver for the GS201 SoC of the Google Pixel 7

The driver 'gs201_platform' hands out the devices of the devices ROM
(board/google_pixel7/devices) to the other drivers. It switches the power
domains, clocks, and supplies that the devices name, the supplies via the
power-management firmware (ACPM).

It is part of every driver scenario of this repository, e.g.,
'run/exynos_fb_pixel'.

With the config attribute 'rtc', it also serves the read-only Rtc session for
the RTC of the S2MPG12 PMIC, which is behind the same firmware. The scenario
'run/rtc_pixel' reads the time:

! make run/rtc_pixel KERNEL=hw BOARD=google_pixel7
